====== Leetcode 152. Maximum Product Subarray (27th Feb)=======
Algorithm for finding maximum product subarray:
Step 1: Initialize two variables:
•	lm (left product) = 1
•	rm (right product) = 1
Step 2: Initialize maxv to the smallest possible integer value.
Step 3: Get the length of the array.
Step 4: Traverse the array from left to right using a loop.
Step 5: At each step:
•	If lm becomes 0, reset it to 1.
•	If rm becomes 0, reset it to 1.
(This is done because multiplying by 0 will make the product 0, so we restart the product.)
Step 6: Multiply lm with the current element from the left side.
Step 7: Multiply rm with the current element from the right side (start from the end and move backward).
Step 8: Compare lm and rm with maxv.
Update maxv with the maximum value among them.
Step 9: Continue this process until all elements are processed.
Step 10: Return maxv.
This gives the maximum product of any continuous subarray.
 Time Complexity = O(n)
Space Complexity = O(1)


                ------------> Code <----------------------
class Solution {
    public int maxProduct(int[] nums) {
        int lm=1,rm=1;
        int n=nums.length;
        int maxv=Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            lm= lm==0 ? 1 :lm;
            rm= rm==0 ? 1 :rm;

            lm=lm*nums[i];
            rm=rm*nums[n-1-i];
            maxv=Math.max(maxv,Math.max(lm,rm));
        }
        return maxv;
    }
}
